```text
needs to be in the dedication statement as the City owns some of the land within the plat boundary.
Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present. (#5897)

RESOLUTION – Authorizing the Mayor and the City Clerk to sign a Final Plat for Clear
Creek Subdivision, 2nd Filing, being situated in portions of Sections 11 and 12, Township 13 North,
Range 67 West of the Sixth Principal Meridian, City of Cheyenne, Wyoming (located southeast
of the I-25 and I-80 interchange).  Mr. Roybal, seconded by Mr. Case, moved to adopt with revised
plat map and the following staff conditions:  #1 – Include the Mayor’s and City Clerk’s names and
titles on the signature block in the dedication statement, and #2 – Provide dimensional data for the
40 ft. access easement or provide a reference book and page if this access easement follows a pre-
existing easement.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.
(#5898)

RESOLUTION – Acknowledging receipt of the Southeast Greenway Trail Connector Plan.
Mr. Roybal moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. White.  Comment was made on project
improvements of this type, the need to find funding for the project and the importance of receiving
over-the-cap funding from the state to help the City with costs of community growth and affiliated
needs.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present. (#5899)

RESOLUTION – Acknowledging receipt of the Cheyenne Frontier Days Traffic Study and
Transportation Plan.  Mr. Roybal moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. White.  Discussion included
support of the plan; extensive use of the area during Frontier Days celebrations; the need to find
funding for the project and the importance of receiving over-the-cap funding from the state, and
implementation of the plan to assist with law enforcement officer safety.  Motion carried.  Voting
“yes” – all members of the governing body present. (#5900)

[CA]
RESOLUTION – Authorizing the Mayor and City Clerk to execute a State Historic
Preservation Office Certified Local Government Grant Agreement for board training to attend two
historic preservation conferences.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried. (#5901)

[CA]
RESOLUTION – Certifying that the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne has agreed
upon the Laramie County Sheriff Detention Center Pump Project, to be submitted to the State Loan
and Investment Board for 2015-2016 Countywide Consensus Block Grant Funding.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried. (#5902)

[CA]
RESOLUTION – Designating local banks as depositories for municipal funds – referred
to Finance Committee. (Sponsor – Mr. Luna)

[CA]
Memorandum of Understanding between the City of Cheyenne and Cheyenne Firefighters
Local Union No. 279, International Association of Firefighters to clarify the intent of a portion of
Section 23, Working in a Higher Job Rank, contained in the 2017-2018 Collective Labor
Agreement.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried. (#6768)

[CA]
Service Agreement between the City of Cheyenne, Community Recreation and Events
Department, and Wyoming Beverage, Cheyenne, Wyoming, for non-alcoholic beverage
concessions for the Ice and Events Center – referred to Finance Committee.
