### Page 5 of 5

```text
Jeff Dierksen referenced comments he made at the last City Council meeting regarding
traffic and safety concerns on Pinto Lane; summarized neighborhood concerns, and reviewed
petitions signed by residents in the neighborhood that had been submitted.  Also under other
business, Dr. Rinne commented the City must follow WYDOT rules and regulations with regard
to altering speed limits, and Mr. Laybourn discussed city-wide traffic and safety concerns.

Mr. Laybourn commented on topics discussed during a meeting that had been held between
the Mayor and Ward I City Council members regarding the Civic Center Commons Project.  Mayor
Orr provided information in response to the comments, noting a new City Engineer will be on
board in January, and advised of the Project’s design status and anticipated timing for issuance of
request for bids.

Mr. Johnson expressed concerns regarding the process utilized for determining the City
Council President and Vice-President for 2018, and with meeting procedures during the current
meeting.

Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk, stated, due to timeliness, a resolution was being introduced
under other business entitled: A Resolution supporting the City of Cheyenne’s continuing
participation in the State Small Business Credit Initiative (SSBCI) and Wyoming Smart Capital
Network (WSCN) program; approving program changes through an amendment to the Services
Agreement, including geographic boundaries, board, and the Credit Guaranty and Seed Capital
Network Program, and retaining the majority of the original SSBCI rules as modified by the
WSCN (Sponsor – Mr. Luna).  Mayor Orr referred the resolution to Finance Committee.

There being no further business to come before the governing body, the meeting was
officially adjourned at 6:52 p.m.

Submitted by,

Carol Intlekofer, MMC

City Clerk

This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.

Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle

January 3, 2018
```
